.\" Manpage for mu2e-ssh-setup
.\" Install with: cp mu2e-ssh-setup.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH MU2E\-SSH\-SETUP 1 "2026-07-28" "mu2e-ssh-setup 1.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.
.SH NAME
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \- generate a personalized Mu2e DAQ ssh client configuration
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2e\-ssh\-setup
.RB [ \-\-interactive | \-\-batch ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-fnal\-user
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-key\-default
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-layout
.IR LAYOUT ]
.RI [ options ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2e\-ssh\-setup
builds an ssh client configuration for the Mu2e DAQ machines from the templates
in
.IR templates/ ,
substituting the user's account names and key paths.
The generated configuration teaches
.BR ssh (1)
about the Mu2e gateways, the MC\-2 and MC\-1 nodes, the IERC test stands and the
git servers, so that a command such as
.B ssh mu2edaq09
connects through the correct gateway as the correct user with the correct key.
.PP
The templates themselves contain no personal information and are safe to keep in
version control.
.PP
The script runs on macOS, Linux and Windows with any Python 3.9 or newer, and
requires no third\-party modules.
.BR PyYAML (3)
is used for
.B \-\-config\-file
when present; otherwise a built\-in parser handles the same file.
.
.SS Output modes
Three modes control where the result is left.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the plan. Nothing is written anywhere.
.TP
.I (default)
Write to
.I ./mu2e\-ssh\-config
for inspection. The live ssh directory is not touched.
.TP
.B \-\-install
Write into the live ssh directory, backing up anything already present.
.PP
.B \-\-install
is the only mode that can alter an existing configuration, and it backs up
first. See
.B SAFETY
below.
.
.SS Layouts
.TP
.B include
A main
.I config
plus one file per host group, pulled in with the
.B Include
keyword. Requires OpenSSH 7.3 or newer. This is the default on macOS and Linux.
.TP
.B monolithic
A single self\-contained
.IR config .
Required by clients that do not implement
.BR Include ,
such as PuTTY and older Git\-for\-Windows bundles. This is the default on
Windows.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Mode
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Prompt for each setting. This is the default when no identifying option is
given.
.TP
.B \-\-batch
Never prompt. Fail if a required value is missing.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be written and change nothing on disk. Takes precedence over
.BR \-\-install .
.TP
.B \-\-install
Write into the ssh directory rather than staging in
.IR ./mu2e\-ssh\-config .
.TP
.B \-\-diff
With
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
show a unified diff against the existing files.
.TP
.B \-\-print
With
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
print the generated files in full.
.
.SS Accounts
.TP
.BI \-\-fnal\-user " NAME"
Fermilab services username. Required unless running interactively.
.TP
.BI \-\-github\-user " NAME"
GitHub username. Defaults to
.BR \-\-fnal\-user .
Used only in a comment, since
.I github.com
always authenticates as the ssh user
.BR git .
.TP
.BI \-\-daq\-account " NAME"
Shared account on the DAQ machines. Default
.BR mu2edaq .
.TP
.BI \-\-shift\-account " NAME"
Shared account for control room shifts. Default
.BR mu2eshift .
.TP
.BI \-\-dcs\-account " NAME"
Shared account on the DCS nodes. Default
.BR mu2edcs .
.
.SS Key files
Paths must name the
.B private
key, that is the file
.I without
the
.I .pub
suffix.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-default " PATH"
Key used for the Mu2e DAQ hosts. If omitted, the script looks for
.IR id_ed25519 ,
.I id_rsa
or
.I id_ecdsa
under
.I ~/.ssh/keys/default
and then
.IR ~/.ssh .
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-github " PATH"
Key for
.IR github.com .
Defaults to
.BR \-\-key\-default .
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-fnal " PATH"
Key for
.IR hepcloud\-git.fnal.gov .
Defaults to
.BR \-\-key\-default .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify\-keys
Do not check that the key files exist. Useful when preparing a configuration for
a machine whose keys are not yet in place.
.
.SS Layout and paths
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " {include,monolithic}"
Output layout. Default
.B include
except on Windows, where it is
.BR monolithic .
.TP
.BI \-\-groups " LIST"
Comma\-separated host groups to enable:
.BR mu2edaq ,
.BR controlroom ,
.BR mu2egpvm ,
.BR novagpvm ,
.BR dunegpvm ,
.BR github .
Default
.BR mu2edaq,mu2egpvm,github .
The three
.B gpvm
groups configure the offline interactive nodes
.RI ( mu2egpvm01\-07 ,
.IR novagpvm01\-12 ,
.IR dunegpvm01\-16 ),
which are reached directly, as the user's own account, and accept
.B only
Kerberos authentication. Their blocks therefore request GSSAPI even under
.BR \-\-no\-gssapi ,
and the agent is not forwarded to them because they are shared multi\-user
machines.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-groups
Enable every host group.
.TP
.BI \-\-gateway\-precedence " {daq,shift}"
When both the
.B mu2edaq
and
.B controlroom
groups are enabled, both match
.RB \(lq Host
.BR mu2egateway* \(rq
with different accounts.
.BR ssh (1)
honours the first match; this selects which. Default
.BR daq .
.TP
.B \-\-user\-config\-first
Include
.I config_other
before the Mu2e groups so that the user's own settings take precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-dir " DIR"
The ssh directory the generated files refer to. Default
.IR ~/.ssh .
.TP
.BI \-\-output\-dir " DIR"
Where to write. Default
.IR ./mu2e\-ssh\-config ,
or the ssh directory with
.BR \-\-install .
.TP
.BI \-\-backup\-dir " DIR"
Where to place backups. Default
.IR <ssh\-dir>/backup\-<timestamp> .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-backup
Do not back up existing files. Intended for scripted rebuilds of disposable
machines.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Do not ask before replacing existing files. Required by
.B \-\-batch
when files are already present.
.TP
.BI \-\-templates\-dir " DIR"
Directory holding the
.I .template
files. Default
.I templates/
beside the script.
.TP
.BI \-c ", " \-\-config\-file " FILE"
Read settings from a YAML file. See
.B FILES
below.
.
.SS Host settings
.TP
.BI \-\-mc2\-gateway " HOST"
Gateway for the MC\-2 machines. Default
.IR mu2egateway01.fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-\-ierc\-gateway " HOST"
Gateway for the IERC test stands. Default
.IR mu2edaq\-gateway.fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-\-kerberos\-realm " REALM"
Realm used to build the example
.BR kinit (1)
command in the comments of the gpvm files. Default
.BR FNAL.GOV .
This does not affect authentication, which takes the realm from
.IR /etc/krb5.conf .
.TP
.BI \-\-canonical\-domain " DOMAIN"
Domain appended to bare hostnames. Default
.IR fnal.gov .
.TP
.BI \-\-strict\-host\-key\-checking " {yes,no,ask,accept\-new}"
.B StrictHostKeyChecking
policy for the generated configuration. Default
.BR accept\-new ,
which trusts a host key on first use and refuses it if it later changes.
.
.SS Features
Each feature has a negative form, for example
.BR \-\-no\-x11 .
.TP
.B \-\-keychain
Store key passphrases in the macOS keychain. On by default on macOS, forced off
elsewhere.
.TP
.B \-\-gssapi
Kerberos/GSSAPI authentication to fnal.gov hosts. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-x11
X11 forwarding, needed for otsdaq GUIs and DAQ Interface windows. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-agent
Forward the ssh agent to remote hosts, so that an onward hop from a gateway can
use the same key. On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-canonicalize
Let bare names such as
.I mu2edaq09
resolve to
.IR mu2edaq09.fnal.gov .
On by default.
.TP
.B \-\-controlmaster
Reuse a single TCP connection for repeat logins to the same host. Off by
default.
.
.SS Validation and output
.TP
.B \-\-no\-validate
Skip running
.B ssh \-G
against the generated configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable coloured output.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.
.SH SAFETY
.B mu2e\-ssh\-setup
does not silently replace an existing ssh configuration.
.IP \(bu 3
Any existing file that would change is copied to a timestamped backup directory
before being replaced. Nothing is overwritten in place.
.IP \(bu 3
Existing files are listed, with size and modification time, before anything is
written.
.IP \(bu 3
Interactively, the user is asked to confirm, and declining is the default. In
.B \-\-batch
mode the script exits with status 2 and changes nothing unless
.B \-\-force
is given.
.IP \(bu 3
.I config_other
is created only if absent and is never overwritten, so personal host entries
survive regeneration.
.IP \(bu 3
Re\-running with unchanged settings is a no\-op; the timestamp in the generated
header is ignored when comparing, so no spurious backup is made.
.IP \(bu 3
Every referenced key file is checked for existence before anything is written.
Keys that are group\- or world\-readable, or that appear to be public keys,
produce a warning.
.IP \(bu 3
The result is parsed with
.B ssh \-G
before the script reports success.
.
.SH CONFIGURATION PRECEDENCE
Settings are merged from four sources, each overriding the ones before it:
.PP
.RS 4
built\-in defaults < \-\-config\-file < MU2E_SSH_* environment < command line
.RE
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2E_SSH_*
Any setting may be supplied as an environment variable named
.B MU2E_SSH_
followed by the uppercased setting name, for example
.B MU2E_SSH_FNAL_USER
or
.BR MU2E_SSH_LAYOUT .
.TP
.B MU2E_SSH_PYTHON
Consulted by the
.IR mu2e\-ssh\-setup.sh ,
.I .cmd
and
.I .ps1
wrappers to select a specific Python interpreter.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables coloured output, as does
.BR \-\-no\-color .
.
.SH FILES
Within the
.I Bootstrap/ssh
directory of the mu2edaq distribution:
.TP
.I scripts/mu2e\-ssh\-setup.py
The generator itself.
.TP
.IR scripts/mu2e\-ssh\-setup.sh ", " scripts/mu2e\-ssh\-setup.cmd ", " scripts/mu2e\-ssh\-setup.ps1
Wrappers that locate a suitable Python interpreter and forward all arguments.
Use the
.I .sh
wrapper on macOS and Linux, and either of the other two on Windows.
.TP
.I templates/*.template
Source templates. Substitution tokens have the form
.BR @@NAME@@ ;
lines beginning with
.B #@
are template directives and never appear in the output. Located automatically
relative to the script, so it may be invoked from any working directory.
.TP
.I examples/mu2e\-ssh\-setup.yaml
Fully commented example configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
Main generated configuration.
.TP
.IR ~/.ssh/config_mu2edaq ", " ~/.ssh/config_mu2e_controlroom ", " ~/.ssh/config_mu2egpvm ", " ~/.ssh/config_novagpvm ", " ~/.ssh/config_dunegpvm ", " ~/.ssh/config_github
Per\-group configurations, in
.B include
layout only.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config_other
Reserved for the user's own entries. Never overwritten.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/backup\-<timestamp>/
Backups of files replaced by a previous run.
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a dry run that completed.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, missing templates, or
.BR ssh (1)
rejected the generated configuration.
.TP
.B 2
Deliberate abort: existing files were found without
.BR \-\-force ,
or a referenced key file is missing.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
Answer the questions and preview the result without writing anything:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-interactive \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install for a named user, backing up whatever is present:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-fnal\-user jdoe \\
    \-\-key\-default ~/.ssh/keys/default/id_ed25519 \\
    \-\-key\-github  ~/.ssh/keys/github/id_ed25519 \\
    \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.PP
See exactly what would change before committing to it:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-fnal\-user jdoe \-\-dry\-run \-\-diff
.fi
.RE
.PP
Produce a single self\-contained file for a client that cannot follow
.BR Include :
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-fnal\-user jdoe \-\-layout monolithic \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.PP
Control room shifter who does not need DAQ access:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-fnal\-user jdoe \-\-groups controlroom \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.PP
An offline analyst who wants only the interactive nodes, across all three
experiments:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-fnal\-user jdoe \\
    \-\-groups mu2egpvm,novagpvm,dunegpvm,github \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unattended installation from a shared configuration file:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mu2e\-ssh\-setup \-\-config\-file /nfs/mu2e/site\-ssh.yaml \\
    \-\-batch \-\-force \-\-install
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR ssh\-agent (1),
.BR ssh\-add (1),
.BR kinit (1)
.PP
